# Record the details

A notebook makes an experiment easier to understand and repeat. Record the setup, the measurements, and the choices you make.

## A simple example

Write observations separately from interpretations. “The strip bent 4 mm” is an observation; an explanation comes afterward.

**Useful relationship:** total time = trials × time per trial

## Pause and try

Write one observation and one possible interpretation of a simple experiment.

